        "source": "arxiv",
        "title": "Fact or Fiction: Verifying Scientific Claims",
        "abstract": "Verifying scientific claims requires domain expertise to parse technical language and assess whether experimental findings entail or refute a hypothesis. We present SciFact, a dataset of 1,409 expert-written scientific claims paired with evidence-containing abstracts annotated with SUPPORTS, REFUTES, or NOT_ENOUGH_INFO labels and rationale sentences. Baseline pipeline systems that retrieve evidence via lexical BM25 alone miss 23.4% of multi-hop rationale spans where terminology shifts between the claim and the abstract. Combining dense retrieval with sentence-level rationale selection boosts label Macro-F1 by 9.8 points.",
